{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows atropine sulfate injection has been in shortage since 2012-01-01 with multiple manufacturers listed as Current, including Hospira, Inc. and American Regent, Inc., whose registered plants have prior OAI inspections.",
  "headline_cites": ["D9", "E48", "E44", "E11", "E13", "E15", "E27"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage database records the first posting for atropine sulfate injection on 2012-01-01 and the shortage remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D9", "E48"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The list includes Hospira, Inc. (package NDC 0409-1630-10) with a related info note of manufacturing delay and next delivery estimated December 2026.",
      "cites": ["E48"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira's registered plant (FEI 1021343) received OAI classifications on 2010-01-19, 2011-06-17, and 2011-08-04, and a Warning Letter on 2010-04-12.",
      "cites": ["E11", "E13", "E15", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "American Regent, Inc. (package NDC 0517-1001-25) is also listed Current with initial posting 2012-01-01.",
      "cites": ["E44"]
    },
    {
      "text": "American Regent's registered plant (FEI 2410375) received an OAI classification on 2011-03-15 and a Warning Letter on 2011-08-31.",
      "cites": ["E27", "E34"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our supply of 0.1 mg/mL 10 mL syringes (NDC 00409163010) is labeled by Hospira, Inc. at both Corvale East and Corvale General.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked mitigation per rule is to transfer 10 syringes of 0.1 mg/mL 10 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 1.8 to 5 days on hand while Corvale General remains above two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D10", "D1", "D2"]
    }
  ]
}
